    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2022-tame-05: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.10";
    dc:description "The statement is a rule for attributing agency: use whichever model gives the most efficient prediction and control. Experiments can rank models, and the ranking cannot come out against the rule, because the rule defines the preferred level as the winner. That is a methodological stipulation rather than a result public data could refute.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Model comparison can rank which description predicts and controls a system most efficiently, and under this claim the winner is the correct agency level by definition.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Every outcome of a predictive comparison is compatible with the claim, because the claim stipulates that the best-controlling model is the right level of agency.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.82"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.098"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
